<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.339 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.339 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.9 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due January 16, 1997 was 3.339 percent, down from 3.465 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.3 billion of 175-day T-bills due April 10, 1997 was 3.571 percent, down from 3.706 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due October 16 was 3.728 percent, down from 3.996 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$800 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.15 billion of C$5.0 billion of bills due Oct 24. (Details follow)  </p>
